I encountered an issue during testing for a planned conversion from Sakai 23 to Sakai 25. This may be of interest to other institutes - I assume it is possible others _could possibly_ have user preference samigoOpen values in similar state to ones we have found in our Sakai 23 database.  



Sakai 25 / 26 the user preference for whether to be notified upon an assessment’s open time is saved in SAKAI_PREFERENCES.XML table/column in an XML element saki.:
{{   <prefs key="noti:types:sakai:samigoOpen">}}

{{       <properties>}}

{{           <property enc="BASE64" name="2" value="Mg=="/>}}

{{       </properties>}}

{{   </prefs>}}

At our institute in Sakai 23 database we have encountered some users where this property has an empty string (cause of this is unknown):
{{   <prefs key="noti:types:sakai:samigoOpen">}}

{{       <properties>}}

{{           <property enc="BASE64" name="2" value=""/>}}

{{       </properties>}}

{{   </prefs>}}

When testing for our planned Sakai 23 to Sakai 25 conversion we discovered that users with an empty string in the samigoOpen value would cause a silent exception when the user was to receive a Sakai 25 email assessment notification. This exception had the effect of preventing any notification for the assessment from being emailed.



I then tested in a local instance of Sakai 26 OOTB.

In Sakai23 that value is not read - notifications go out at time of publication. In Sakai 25/26 the notification job reads this preference value and attempts to parse it as an integer. When the value is an empty string ({{""}}), the job fails with a {{NumberFormatException}}, which prevents *any* email notifications from being sent for that assessment.

We confirmed this behavior in the local *Sakai 26 OOTB* environment.

see:   samigo/samigo-impl/src/java/org/sakaiproject/samigo/impl/SamigoAvailableNotificationServiceImpl.java

exception occurs here:
    224        int noti = Integer.parseInt(notiStr);
    225         if (noti == NotificationService.PREF_IGNORE) {
    226             log.debug("Skipping notification to user because of user preference override: {}", userNow.getEid());
    227             return;
    228         }

In our case:

* ~94 user accounts currently have this invalid {{samigoOpen}} preference in our Sakai 23 database
* In our test Sakai 26 OOTB instance toggling the notification preference *off → save → on → save* rewrites the XML with a valid value and resolves the issue for that user account

This is the query I used against a copy of our Sakai 23 production database to identify the affected Tests & Quizzes preference entries:

{{SELECT suim.EID, suim.*, sp.*}}

{{FROM SAKAI_PREFERENCES sp}}

{{JOIN SAKAI_USER_ID_MAP suim}}

{{  ON sp.PREFERENCES_ID = suim.USER_ID}}

{{WHERE XML LIKE '%<prefs key="noti:types:sakai:samigoOpen">%<properties>%<property enc="BASE64" name="2" value=""/>%'}}

{{ORDER BY suim.EID;}}

I don’t yet know the cause of the empty value string, but safeguarding the 25/26 code against this silent exception/notification failure might be advisable.

Thoughts?

