When a Turnitin classic standard assignment is created within Sakai, the content item json received by Turnitin is stored within the contentitem record in the lti_content database. This json consistently contains a “submissionReview” property within its “lineItem” property per the example snippet that follows:

{noformat}  "lineItem":{
      "scoreMaximum":100,
      "gradesReleased":false,
      "tag":"grade",
      "submissionReview":{
         "reviewableStatus":[
            "Submitted"
         ]
      }
    },{noformat}

For Turnitin new standard assignments, the “submissionReview” property is absent, per the following example snippet:

{noformat}  "lineItem":{
      "scoreMaximum":100,
      "gradesReleased":false,
      "tag":"grade"
   },{noformat}

Per the LTI Submission Review Service specification ([https://www.imsglobal.org/spec/lti-sr/v1p0|https://www.imsglobal.org/spec/lti-sr/v1p0|smart-link] ), Sakai is expecting a “submissionReview” property for the proper launch URL within Sakai’s Assignment Grader to reach the proper student submission (the Feedback Studio report for a given student instead of the generic instructor panel for the assignment in Turnitin). Refer to the test plan for details.

It seems like an expedient solution to this would be for Turnitin to implement for new standard assignments what is currently generating the submissionReview attribute for classic standard assignments.

